Patch-Id: ASTRA-0001
Title: Wire Astra overlay dir into the browser app build
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: browser/app.mozbuild
Intent: include /astra (overlay: chrome://astra/, resource://astra/) in the build; no configure option can add a new top-level dir, so a hook is required
Risk: low (one DIRS line before /browser; upstream rarely reorders this file)
Test: forge overlay + forge lint; configure proof in UPSTREAM.md; full-build proof in P1-T04
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: none anticipated; drop if upstream ever supports out-of-tree app dirs
---
diff --git a/browser/app.mozbuild b/browser/app.mozbuild
index 04cfef370d..2487a3dc81 100644
--- a/browser/app.mozbuild
+++ b/browser/app.mozbuild
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@ include("/toolkit/toolkit.mozbuild")
 
 DIRS += ["/%s" % CONFIG["MOZ_BRANDING_DIRECTORY"]]
 
+# ASTRA-0001: include the Astra overlay (chrome://astra/, resource://astra/).
+# Must precede /browser (dirs after browser are not packaged properly on Mac).
+DIRS += ["/astra"]
+
 # Never add dirs after browser because they apparently won't get
 # packaged properly on Mac.
 DIRS += ["/browser"]
